WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.773
Retrieval-augmented generation and memory
features can strongly influence agent

2
00:00:07.853 --> 00:00:08.775
behavior.

3
00:00:08.855 --> 00:00:15.514
The agent may query a vector store,
retrieve documents, consult prior notes,

4
00:00:15.594 --> 00:00:21.843
read user-specific memory, or write new
memory for later interactions.

5
00:00:21.923 --> 00:00:28.684
Monitoring needs to show what information
influenced the response or action.

6
00:00:28.764 --> 00:00:34.603
If the agent cites a policy, recommends a
change, or takes an action,

7
00:00:34.683 --> 00:00:41.034
investigators should be able to see the
source path behind that behavior.

8
00:00:41.114 --> 00:00:45.929
Source provenance is central to retrieval
monitoring.

9
00:00:46.009 --> 00:00:50.926
Logs should identify where retrieved
content came from,

10
00:00:51.006 --> 00:00:58.074
which tenant or workspace it belonged to,
when it was accessed, and how it was used.

11
00:00:58.154 --> 00:01:05.325
Source references are more durable and
privacy-aware than storing full retrieved

12
00:01:05.405 --> 00:01:06.941
text in every log.

13
00:01:07.021 --> 00:01:11.529
They also help analysts detect stale,
conflicting,

14
00:01:11.609 --> 00:01:17.448
or unauthorized sources that may have
affected the agent's output.

15
00:01:17.528 --> 00:01:23.367
Memory requires special care because it
can shape future behavior.

16
00:01:23.447 --> 00:01:28.569
Memory reads should be visible when they
affect a response.

17
00:01:28.649 --> 00:01:34.590
Memory writes should be monitored because
they may store sensitive,

18
00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:38.973
incorrect, stale, or unauthorized
information.

19
00:01:39.053 --> 00:01:43.867
Memory deletion should also be recorded
when relevant.

20
00:01:43.947 --> 00:01:49.377
Cross-user or cross-tenant memory exposure
is a serious risk,

21
00:01:49.457 --> 00:01:55.501
so monitoring should confirm that
isolation boundaries are working.

22
00:01:55.581 --> 00:02:01.932
Retrieved content can also carry untrusted
instructions at a high level.

23
00:02:02.012 --> 00:02:09.285
Monitoring should help teams identify when
external content influenced tool use or

24
00:02:09.365 --> 00:02:11.926
policy-sensitive behavior.

25
00:02:12.006 --> 00:02:18.562
The system does not need to log every
token of protected content to be useful.

26
00:02:18.642 --> 00:02:24.891
It does need to record the source, access
decision, redaction decision,

27
00:02:24.971 --> 00:02:31.220
and relationship between retrieved
context, model output, and action.
